1
00:00:07,183 --> 00:00:08,883
Listen to a sound nearby.

2
00:00:08,963 --> 00:00:12,062
A car, a bird, the hum of a fridge.

3
00:00:12,142 --> 00:00:16,021
It is vivid and clear, and
it needs no help to be known.

4
00:00:16,825 --> 00:00:22,275
Every step of the logic looks at
something. A self. An object. A cause.

5
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:24,041
Matter. A person.

6
00:00:24,121 --> 00:00:28,103
It is easy to hear these as
many topics, one after another.

7
00:00:28,183 --> 00:00:29,775
They are not many topics.

8
00:00:29,855 --> 00:00:33,103
Each time, the logic is
looking at a phenomenon.

9
00:00:33,183 --> 00:00:35,105
What Buddhism calls a dharma.

10
00:00:35,909 --> 00:00:41,023
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

11
00:00:41,854 --> 00:00:44,111
So first, what is a phenomenon?

12
00:00:44,191 --> 00:00:46,299
In Buddhism the answer is simple.

13
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:49,886
A phenomenon is whatever
can be experienced or known.

14
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:53,853
A sound, a colour, a hardness, a feeling,

15
00:00:53,933 --> 00:00:55,964
a thought, an intention.

16
00:00:56,066 --> 00:00:59,288
Things only thought of,
like a number or a plan.

17
00:00:59,368 --> 00:01:05,062
And the knowing too: a moment of seeing
is itself a dharma. Nothing is left out.

18
00:01:05,142 --> 00:01:06,629
Everything is dharma.

19
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:09,482
The tradition sorts them in two.

20
00:01:09,562 --> 00:01:13,626
Conditioned dharmas arise
from conditions and pass:

21
00:01:13,706 --> 00:01:17,131
every sight, every sound, every thought.

22
00:01:17,211 --> 00:01:20,745
Unconditioned dharmas are
not made by conditions:

23
00:01:20,825 --> 00:01:26,058
in the old lists, space, and
nirvāṇa, the ceasing of suffering.

24
00:01:26,138 --> 00:01:29,962
Conditioned or unconditioned,
they are all dharmas.

25
00:01:30,774 --> 00:01:33,154
The word comes from a
root meaning to hold.

26
00:01:33,234 --> 00:01:37,393
The Abhidharma teachers said a
dharma is what holds its own mark.

27
00:01:37,473 --> 00:01:40,015
Hardness for earth. Heat for fire.

28
00:01:40,095 --> 00:01:41,713
Knowing for consciousness.

29
00:01:41,793 --> 00:01:45,667
They had seen through the
self, the person, the chariot.

30
00:01:45,747 --> 00:01:49,557
But they kept the dharmas as the
pieces the world is built of,

31
00:01:49,674 --> 00:01:51,482
each holding its own nature.

32
00:01:51,562 --> 00:01:56,446
No self in the person, but the pieces
still standing from their own side.

33
00:01:57,261 --> 00:02:01,012
Nāgārjuna turned the search
on the dharmas themselves.

34
00:02:01,092 --> 00:02:03,499
Not even a dharma holds its own mark.

35
00:02:03,579 --> 00:02:05,822
Searched for, it is not found.

36
00:02:05,902 --> 00:02:08,322
It arises only in dependence.

37
00:02:08,402 --> 00:02:10,836
And the unconditioned gets no exemption.

38
00:02:10,916 --> 00:02:13,865
Since the conditioned is
not established at all,

39
00:02:13,945 --> 00:02:16,990
he asks, how could the unconditioned be?

40
00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:23,070
Space, nirvāṇa, even emptiness
itself: dharmas too, and empty too.

41
00:02:24,134 --> 00:02:26,269
This is what after anatta means.

42
00:02:26,349 --> 00:02:30,644
The same seeing that found no self
is turned on every phenomenon.

43
00:02:30,724 --> 00:02:33,814
Every dharma is vivid, and not found.

44
00:02:34,626 --> 00:02:38,405
So the self is dharmas:
the sights, sounds,

45
00:02:38,485 --> 00:02:43,813
sensations and thoughts of this moment,
mistaken for someone standing behind them.

46
00:02:43,893 --> 00:02:48,745
An object is dharmas again, mistaken
for a thing out there on its own.

47
00:02:48,825 --> 00:02:51,530
Cause, matter and person are the same.

48
00:02:51,610 --> 00:02:54,750
The steps do not move from
one subject to another.

49
00:02:54,830 --> 00:02:58,717
They look at this one vivid
appearing, from different sides,

50
00:02:58,797 --> 00:03:02,064
until the habit of making it
into things is seen through.

51
00:03:02,865 --> 00:03:05,774
Now the second point,
and it is easy to miss.

52
00:03:05,854 --> 00:03:11,046
We usually picture two layers. First a
bare appearance. Then a name put on it.

53
00:03:11,126 --> 00:03:16,005
The logic then seems to be about names,
and the appearance sits underneath,

54
00:03:16,085 --> 00:03:18,953
simply given. That picture is still dual.

55
00:03:19,033 --> 00:03:22,653
It keeps a raw given under
the label, one more floor.

56
00:03:23,474 --> 00:03:27,104
There is no bare appearance
underneath, waiting to be named.

57
00:03:27,184 --> 00:03:30,392
Designation is not a label
put on the appearing.

58
00:03:30,472 --> 00:03:33,168
The appearing itself is the designation.

59
00:03:33,977 --> 00:03:37,728
How can that be? Because
designation needs no words.

60
00:03:37,808 --> 00:03:42,742
It needs only singling out. This
sound. This colour. This ache.

61
00:03:42,822 --> 00:03:46,424
Picked out as this. A baby
does it. A bird does it.

62
00:03:46,504 --> 00:03:48,571
We do it long before any word.

63
00:03:48,651 --> 00:03:51,437
The Buddha's own word
for it is recognising:

64
00:03:51,517 --> 00:03:53,380
picking out a mark as this.

65
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:55,717
Whatever appears is already a this.

66
00:03:55,797 --> 00:03:58,072
So nothing appears undesignated.

67
00:03:58,893 --> 00:04:01,421
And singling out is already dependence.

68
00:04:01,501 --> 00:04:04,275
A this stands out only
against what it is not.

69
00:04:04,355 --> 00:04:07,875
Only with this seeing,
this light, this attention.

70
00:04:07,955 --> 00:04:10,959
Take away the background,
and nothing stands out.

71
00:04:11,039 --> 00:04:14,374
Take away the conditions,
and nothing is singled out.

72
00:04:15,206 --> 00:04:17,821
Picture a world where there is only blue:

73
00:04:17,910 --> 00:04:22,816
one hue, everywhere, and nothing
else. No one there would see blue.

74
00:04:22,896 --> 00:04:27,028
Nothing would let it stand out, so it
would never be singled out as blue.

75
00:04:27,108 --> 00:04:29,148
We would be blind to blueness.

76
00:04:29,228 --> 00:04:31,815
Blue is seen only with what is not blue.

77
00:04:32,621 --> 00:04:37,133
Now let one other colour appear
in that world: a spot of red.

78
00:04:37,213 --> 00:04:42,744
At once both appear, blue and
red, each bright and unmistakable.

79
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:47,092
This simple example shows how the key
points we meet again and again come

80
00:04:47,172 --> 00:04:49,905
together, if it is clearly understood.

81
00:04:49,985 --> 00:04:53,057
Blue and red don't arise
one after the other.

82
00:04:53,137 --> 00:04:55,806
They arise together, in one stroke.

83
00:04:56,679 --> 00:04:58,787
First, neither comes first.

84
00:04:58,867 --> 00:05:03,134
Blue wasn't sitting there unseen,
waiting for red to reveal it.

85
00:05:03,214 --> 00:05:07,346
Red didn't arrive and then get
compared with a blue already there.

86
00:05:07,426 --> 00:05:11,264
The moment red appears,
blue and red both appear,

87
00:05:11,353 --> 00:05:13,515
each by contrast with the other.

88
00:05:13,595 --> 00:05:18,248
Like seer and seen, long
and short, here and there:

89
00:05:18,337 --> 00:05:20,707
named together, neither prior.

90
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:24,276
Second, dependence isn't a sequence.

91
00:05:24,356 --> 00:05:28,896
We usually picture dependence as something
waiting on something else in time:

92
00:05:28,976 --> 00:05:32,795
first the cause, then the
effect. Here nothing waits.

93
00:05:32,875 --> 00:05:36,586
The dependence is in the
appearing itself, all at once.

94
00:05:36,666 --> 00:05:39,073
This is the logic of the single stroke.

95
00:05:39,153 --> 00:05:44,073
The parts, their relations and their
naming do not arise in sequence.

96
00:05:44,153 --> 00:05:47,487
They are aspects of one
dependently arisen event.

97
00:05:48,359 --> 00:05:53,347
Third, each colour is empty,
and vivid, at the same moment.

98
00:05:53,427 --> 00:05:55,698
Blue has no blueness of its own.

99
00:05:55,778 --> 00:05:57,871
Alone, it isn't even seen.

100
00:05:57,951 --> 00:06:02,708
Yet the instant red is there,
blue is bright and unmistakable.

101
00:06:02,788 --> 00:06:07,631
Being empty and being vivid aren't
two stages. They are one appearing.

102
00:06:08,485 --> 00:06:10,335
Fourth, nothing produced it.

103
00:06:10,415 --> 00:06:14,492
Red didn't make blue appear,
and blue didn't make red appear.

104
00:06:14,572 --> 00:06:16,666
Neither is the cause of the other.

105
00:06:16,746 --> 00:06:19,438
With the meeting, the
whole scene is just there,

106
00:06:19,518 --> 00:06:22,753
already complete, not
built up step by step.

107
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:26,327
That is spontaneous presence
in the plainest example.

108
00:06:26,407 --> 00:06:32,309
Not uncaused, since without the contrast
nothing appears. But not produced either.

109
00:06:33,189 --> 00:06:35,174
Fifth, it isn't one thing either.

110
00:06:35,254 --> 00:06:40,310
Blue and red appearing together doesn't
merge them into one big field of colour

111
00:06:40,390 --> 00:06:43,842
behind both. Each is distinct and clear.

112
00:06:43,922 --> 00:06:48,312
They are neither one nor two:
not separate things that meet,

113
00:06:48,392 --> 00:06:51,075
and not one thing in two shades.

114
00:06:51,893 --> 00:06:55,209
In short: appearing is
relation from the start,

115
00:06:55,289 --> 00:06:59,122
all at once, with nothing
first and nothing behind.

116
00:06:59,202 --> 00:07:03,457
That is why, by appearing,
a thing is already empty.

117
00:07:03,537 --> 00:07:06,613
And why the same appearing
is complete by itself.

118
00:07:07,438 --> 00:07:11,747
So singling out is not something done
to an appearance that was there first.

119
00:07:11,827 --> 00:07:13,486
It is already dependence.

120
00:07:13,566 --> 00:07:16,027
And dependence is already emptiness.

121
00:07:16,107 --> 00:07:18,527
Look for the this apart
from its conditions,

122
00:07:18,607 --> 00:07:22,376
in its parts or apart from
them, and it is not found.

123
00:07:23,197 --> 00:07:25,032
Singling out is dependence.

124
00:07:25,112 --> 00:07:26,935
Dependence is emptiness.

125
00:07:27,015 --> 00:07:30,716
So by appearing, a thing is already empty.

126
00:07:31,529 --> 00:07:34,710
Nothing appears first and
turns out empty later.

127
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:39,098
This is what Nāgārjuna means when
he says that dependent arising,

128
00:07:39,178 --> 00:07:42,060
emptiness and dependent
designation are one.

129
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:44,383
The logic does not make things empty.

130
00:07:44,463 --> 00:07:46,639
It shows what appearing already is.

131
00:07:46,719 --> 00:07:50,457
And it is why Candrakīrti
refuses a bare particular,

132
00:07:50,537 --> 00:07:52,848
given before any designation.

133
00:07:52,928 --> 00:07:55,040
No such bare given is found.

134
00:07:55,845 --> 00:07:57,979
None of this makes the world thin.

135
00:07:58,059 --> 00:08:00,085
Singling out is not the mistake.

136
00:08:00,165 --> 00:08:05,602
A mirror shows every reflection, clear
and distinct, and holds none of them.

137
00:08:05,682 --> 00:08:10,398
The mistake is one step further: taking
what is singled out as standing on its

138
00:08:10,478 --> 00:08:12,463
own, from its own side.

139
00:08:12,543 --> 00:08:15,642
The singling out goes on, vivid and exact.

140
00:08:15,722 --> 00:08:18,745
Only the extra "on its own" is not found.

141
00:08:19,574 --> 00:08:21,084
Take something you can hold.

142
00:08:21,164 --> 00:08:24,644
Someone passes you an apple,
and you hold it in your hand.

143
00:08:24,724 --> 00:08:27,823
It seems plain that you
are holding a solid apple,

144
00:08:27,903 --> 00:08:33,167
out there, on its own, and that the
senses only report on it. Look again.

145
00:08:34,002 --> 00:08:36,558
The hardness is not stored in the apple.

146
00:08:36,638 --> 00:08:42,102
It arises when skin meets fruit, the
fingers press, and touch is there.

147
00:08:42,182 --> 00:08:44,316
Press lightly and it is firm.

148
00:08:44,396 --> 00:08:46,640
Press with the thumb and it gives.

149
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:48,800
To a stone, it is soft.

150
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:51,504
The coolness depends on
the warmth of your hand.

151
00:08:51,584 --> 00:08:55,734
The weight in your palm is a pull
with the earth, met by your arm.

152
00:08:56,553 --> 00:09:00,861
The red depends on light, on the
skin of the fruit, and on the eye.

153
00:09:00,941 --> 00:09:04,897
Under candlelight it turns
orange. At dusk it goes grey.

154
00:09:04,977 --> 00:09:07,098
A bee sees patterns you cannot.

155
00:09:07,178 --> 00:09:10,657
No red is found sitting on
the apple apart from all this.

156
00:09:10,737 --> 00:09:14,752
Yet it appears vividly, whenever
its conditions come together.

157
00:09:15,578 --> 00:09:18,080
The scent needs the air and the breath.

158
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:20,267
With a blocked nose there is none.

159
00:09:20,347 --> 00:09:22,659
The crunch needs teeth and an ear.

160
00:09:22,739 --> 00:09:24,860
It was not waiting inside the apple.

161
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:28,637
The sweetness needs the tongue:
right after brushing your teeth,

162
00:09:28,717 --> 00:09:34,140
it is another apple. Even the word
"apple" comes with memory and language.

163
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:37,781
The thought, this is an
apple, is one more appearing,

164
00:09:37,861 --> 00:09:39,538
with its own conditions.

165
00:09:40,361 --> 00:09:42,862
Each sense gives only its own appearing.

166
00:09:42,942 --> 00:09:47,332
This hardness, this red,
this crunch, this sweetness.

167
00:09:47,412 --> 00:09:50,743
None of them gives an apple
standing out there on its own.

168
00:09:50,823 --> 00:09:55,974
Mental formation, from the habits of
the inherent framework, does the rest.

169
00:09:56,054 --> 00:09:59,479
It ties the appearings
into one solid thing,

170
00:09:59,559 --> 00:10:02,400
as if they all belonged to a hidden core.

171
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:06,712
It puts that thing out there, and
puts a "me" in here, holding it.

172
00:10:07,533 --> 00:10:11,583
Look for the apple apart from its
conditions, and it is not found.

173
00:10:11,663 --> 00:10:13,988
Look for the holder
apart from the holding,

174
00:10:14,068 --> 00:10:17,167
and that is not found
either. Nothing is lost.

175
00:10:17,247 --> 00:10:20,795
You can still eat it, share
it, and plant its seeds.

176
00:10:20,875 --> 00:10:23,499
It works because it is dependently arisen.

177
00:10:23,579 --> 00:10:27,806
An apple that stood on its
own, unchanging and unrelated,

178
00:10:27,886 --> 00:10:32,213
could never ripen, or be
bitten, or feed anyone.

179
00:10:33,038 --> 00:10:34,874
The senses give appearings.

180
00:10:34,954 --> 00:10:37,428
The habit ties them
into an apple out there.

181
00:10:37,508 --> 00:10:42,501
Untied, nothing is missing:
just this, vivid, and light.

182
00:10:43,314 --> 00:10:46,142
The same knot can be told
from the side of light.

183
00:10:46,222 --> 00:10:48,239
The five aggregates are all here.

184
00:10:48,341 --> 00:10:50,888
Form: the hardness, the red.

185
00:10:51,004 --> 00:10:53,370
Feeling: the sweetness is pleasant.

186
00:10:53,450 --> 00:10:57,555
Perception: the shape
recognised as apple. Formations.

187
00:10:57,635 --> 00:11:01,726
And consciousness: touch, seeing, tasting,

188
00:11:01,806 --> 00:11:04,484
each its own stream, unmixed.

189
00:11:04,564 --> 00:11:07,233
The knot is the aggregate of formations.

190
00:11:08,049 --> 00:11:11,474
Dzogchen tells the same
movement from the side of light.

191
00:11:11,554 --> 00:11:15,075
Each aggregate, freed,
is one of five lights.

192
00:11:15,155 --> 00:11:17,643
Grasped as something standing over there,

193
00:11:17,723 --> 00:11:23,050
the lights harden into solid elements,
a solid world, and a solid body.

194
00:11:23,130 --> 00:11:27,507
So the habit that ties the appearings into
an apple out there is the grasping that

195
00:11:27,587 --> 00:11:29,182
hardens the lights.

196
00:11:29,989 --> 00:11:33,554
Untied, the aggregates
are seen as display:

197
00:11:33,684 --> 00:11:39,093
many vivid streams of appearing, with no
core underneath, and no one holding them.

198
00:11:39,173 --> 00:11:42,653
This is also what the
rainbow body is, in essence.

199
00:11:42,733 --> 00:11:45,792
A realization, not the body disappearing.

200
00:11:45,872 --> 00:11:48,822
And the lights are not a
stuff beneath the aggregates.

201
00:11:48,902 --> 00:11:53,011
They name the aggregates' own
clarity, as empty as they are.

202
00:11:53,838 --> 00:11:59,356
Then the clarity. Every appearing
is clear: seen, heard, known.

203
00:11:59,436 --> 00:12:04,343
This clear, vivid knowing is what the
tradition calls the nature of mind,

204
00:12:04,423 --> 00:12:06,068
its luminous clarity.

205
00:12:06,148 --> 00:12:10,525
When it is mistaken, it
becomes me, the one who sees.

206
00:12:10,605 --> 00:12:14,573
When that is seen through,
it is easily mistaken again,

207
00:12:14,653 --> 00:12:19,438
as a capital S Self: a pure
witness, a vast awareness,

208
00:12:19,518 --> 00:12:21,752
the background the world appears in.

209
00:12:22,570 --> 00:12:25,085
But the clarity is the appearing's own.

210
00:12:25,165 --> 00:12:27,558
It is not a light shining from behind.

211
00:12:27,638 --> 00:12:30,561
It too is singled out,
with its conditions,

212
00:12:30,641 --> 00:12:34,678
and searched for, it is not
found apart from what appears.

213
00:12:34,758 --> 00:12:37,286
The seeing is no different from the seen.

214
00:12:37,366 --> 00:12:40,765
Not a seer behind it, and
not found apart from it.

215
00:12:40,845 --> 00:12:44,827
Clear, knowing and empty,
with no one knowing it,

216
00:12:44,907 --> 00:12:46,761
and no ground beneath it.

217
00:12:47,569 --> 00:12:50,899
So when the steps say
designation, hear it this way.

218
00:12:50,979 --> 00:12:53,942
This vivid, clear appearing, singled out,

219
00:12:54,022 --> 00:12:56,076
dependent, and not found.

220
00:12:56,156 --> 00:12:58,988
Awareness is not a second thing beside it.

221
00:12:59,789 --> 00:13:02,440
So the taste and the logic meet here.

222
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:05,537
Direct taste meets the appearing as vivid,

223
00:13:05,617 --> 00:13:08,853
clear and knowing, with no one knowing it.

224
00:13:08,933 --> 00:13:10,972
In seeing, just the seen.

225
00:13:11,052 --> 00:13:15,945
The logic meets the same appearing
and finds nothing standing on its own.

226
00:13:16,025 --> 00:13:17,766
The logic says it is empty.

227
00:13:17,846 --> 00:13:19,763
The taste says it is luminous.

228
00:13:19,843 --> 00:13:24,183
These are not two things, and neither
is a ground beneath the other.

229
00:13:24,993 --> 00:13:29,519
When you look at any phenomenon,
what it actually is, is just this.

230
00:13:29,599 --> 00:13:33,255
Its being not found, and
its arising in dependence.

231
00:13:33,335 --> 00:13:35,936
Not a property it has. What it is.

232
00:13:36,757 --> 00:13:38,783
Try it now. Hear a sound.

233
00:13:38,863 --> 00:13:43,307
Notice it is already this sound,
picked out, before any word.

234
00:13:43,387 --> 00:13:46,541
Notice what it stands out
against, and what it comes with.

235
00:13:46,621 --> 00:13:49,385
Is there a sound left
over, apart from those?

236
00:13:50,214 --> 00:13:53,898
Pick up a piece of fruit. Go
through the senses one by one.

237
00:13:53,978 --> 00:13:57,584
Then look for the fruit apart from
them, and for the one holding it.

238
00:13:58,389 --> 00:14:02,860
Look at your hand. It is already
a hand, singled out, vivid.

239
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:05,700
Look for a hand apart from
its being singled out.

240
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:10,025
Look for the one doing the singling
out. Do not argue. Just look.

241
00:14:10,862 --> 00:14:15,646
Then notice the clarity. Everything
is already known, without effort.

242
00:14:15,726 --> 00:14:17,508
Is the knowing behind the scene?

243
00:14:17,588 --> 00:14:20,433
Or is it just the scene, bright and clear?

244
00:14:21,245 --> 00:14:23,733
Vivid, singled out, dependent.

245
00:14:23,813 --> 00:14:26,210
And by appearing, already empty.

